[
  {
    "44": "If a culture does not respect",
    "45": "its past, it deserves no",
    "46": "future.",
    "47": "",
    "48": "In Kourend, every generation",
    "49": "owes a debt of gratitude and",
    "50": "honour to the previous",
    "51": "generations, recognising",
    "52": "their toil and blood that",
    "53": "raised our kingdom from its",
    "54": "humble origins to its present",
    "55": "glories.",
    "56": "",
    "57": "It has therefore been my",
    "58": "privilege to study the soul",
    "60": "altar, that mystical beacon",
    "61": "that gathers the souls of the",
    "62": "departed, guiding them into",
    "63": "the River.",
    "64": "",
    "65": "My study is no mere academic",
    "66": "interest; I embark on it as a",
    "67": "mark of respect and honour",
    "68": "for the deceased generations",
    "69": "whose souls now flow in the",
    "70": "River.",
    "71": "",
    "72": "The River",
    "73": "",
    "74": "As the mortals of Kourend"
  },
  {
    "44": "reach their death, their",
    "45": "souls abandon the",
    "46": "flesh-temples they inhabited,",
    "47": "leaving the flesh to suffer",
    "48": "corruption and decay.",
    "49": "",
    "50": "The soul, however, does not",
    "51": "decay. Released from the",
    "52": "fetters of its flesh-temple,",
    "53": "and from the constraints of",
    "54": "the material world, the soul",
    "55": "is at last free.",
    "56": "",
    "57": "Mercifully, the soul is not",
    "58": "left to wander aimlessly",
    "60": "through the world. Instead,",
    "61": "the soul altar calls it,",
    "62": "reaching across the land to",
    "63": "all the wandering souls of",
    "64": "Kourend, drawing them to the",
    "65": "River.",
    "66": "",
    "67": "The River leads the souls",
    "68": "through unchartable realms,",
    "69": "transcending the plane of the",
    "70": "world.",
    "71": "",
    "72": "Yet they are not abandoned to",
    "73": "the forces that might prey on",
    "74": "them - the three-headed"
  },
  {
    "44": "Guardian is there as a",
    "45": "protector, keeping them safe",
    "46": "as the River flows beyond all",
    "47": "knowledge.",
    "48": "",
    "49": "The Guardian's Keeper",
    "50": "",
    "51": "Many years ago, before the",
    "52": "Ascent of Arceuus, I was a",
    "53": "young assistant to the",
    "54": "Elders. A day came when there",
    "55": "was terrible turmoil down the",
    "56": "River. A human adventurer had",
    "57": "breached the Guardian's cave;",
    "58": "this broke the bonds of the",
    "60": "Guardian, and she sought to",
    "61": "escape from her solemn duty",
    "62": "of protecting the souls. The",
    "63": "Elders acted fast to restore",
    "64": "the Guardian to her post.",
    "65": "",
    "66": "There was, at that time, a",
    "67": "herbalist whose mind and body",
    "68": "were known to be in a",
    "69": "manipulable state due to his",
    "70": "foolish experiments. Seizing",
    "71": "him while he was helpless in",
    "72": "his potion-induced trance,",
    "73": "the Elders cast spells of",
    "74": "torment upon him; in order to"
  },
